{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Behold now, YHWH has restrained me from bearing.</b> Even though He said He would give you seed, as it says: וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן אֶת הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת (Genesis 12:7) — He did not say that that seed would come from me." "<b>Perhaps I shall be built up from her.</b> Perhaps the jealousy of the womb will arouse the faculty to its activities, and it will be strengthened to achieve seed (Megillah 13)." "<b>To the voice of Sarai.</b> His heart inclined him, so that her judgment would be sound; therefore he accepted her words — not to indulge in the pleasure of the woman."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:22.224093182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}